{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-coordinate-formula","title":"prop:volume-form-coordinate-formula","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":1490,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:volume-form-coordinate-formula","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:volume-form-pointwise]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:frame-matrix]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:wedge-covectors]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-frame-value]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:top-forms-proportional]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:dual-coframe-duality]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:volume-form-coordinate-formula","line":2519,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[Lee 2.41(c): the Coordinate Formula for $dV_g$]\n\\label{prop:volume-form-coordinate-formula}\n\n\\uses{def:volume-form-pointwise, def:frame-matrix, def:wedge-covectors, prop:volume-form-frame-value, lem:top-forms-proportional, lem:dual-coframe-duality}\n\n\n\n\nIf $(Y_i)$ is positively oriented at $x$ and $(\\varepsilon^i)$ is a dual coframe there, then\n\\[\ndV_g|_x=\\sqrt{\\det(g_{ij}(x))}\\,\\varepsilon^1\\wedge\\cdots\\wedge\\varepsilon^n.\n\\]\nThus in oriented coordinates, $dV_g=\\sqrt{\\det(g_{ij})}\\,dx^1\\wedge\\cdots\\wedge dx^n$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{prop:volume-form-frame-value,lem:top-forms-proportional,def:wedge-covectors,lem:dual-coframe-duality}\n\\sketch Both sides are top forms, so compare them on $(Y_i|_x)$. The dual wedge has value $1$ there by Lemma \\ref{lem:dual-coframe-duality}; Proposition \\ref{prop:volume-form-frame-value} gives the same scalar for $dV_g$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[Lee 2.41(c): the Coordinate Formula for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$dV_g$\">$dV_g$</span>] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a766f6c756d652d666f726d2d636f6f7264696e6174652d666f726d756c61\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Avolume-form-pointwise\">↗ def:volume-form-pointwise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Aframe-matrix\">↗ def:frame-matrix</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Awedge-covectors\">↗ def:wedge-covectors</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Avolume-form-frame-value\">↗ prop:volume-form-frame-value</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Atop-forms-proportional\">↗ lem:top-forms-proportional</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Adual-coframe-duality\">↗ lem:dual-coframe-duality</a> <p></p>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(Y_i)$\">$(Y_i)$</span> is positively oriented at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x$\">$x$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(\\varepsilon ^i)$\">$(\\varepsilon ^i)$</span> is a dual coframe there, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  dV_g|_x=\\sqrt{\\det (g_{ij}(x))}\\, \\varepsilon ^1\\wedge \\cdots \\wedge \\varepsilon ^n.  \\]\">\\[  dV_g|_x=\\sqrt{\\det (g_{ij}(x))}\\, \\varepsilon ^1\\wedge \\cdots \\wedge \\varepsilon ^n.  \\]</span> Thus in oriented coordinates, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$dV_g=\\sqrt{\\det (g_{ij})}\\, dx^1\\wedge \\cdots \\wedge dx^n$\">$dV_g=\\sqrt{\\det (g_{ij})}\\, dx^1\\wedge \\cdots \\wedge dx^n$</span>.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Avolume-form-frame-value\">↗ prop:volume-form-frame-value</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Atop-forms-proportional\">↗ lem:top-forms-proportional</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Awedge-covectors\">↗ def:wedge-covectors</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Adual-coframe-duality\">↗ lem:dual-coframe-duality</a> \\sketch Both sides are top forms, so compare them on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(Y_i|_x)$\">$(Y_i|_x)$</span>. The dual wedge has value <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$1$\">$1$</span> there by Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Adual-coframe-duality\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:dual-coframe-duality\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6475616c2d636f6672616d652d6475616c697479\">12</a>; Proposition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Avolume-form-frame-value\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-frame-value\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a766f6c756d652d666f726d2d6672616d652d76616c7565\">12</a> gives the same scalar for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$dV_g$\">$dV_g$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-frame-value","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-volume-form","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:volume-form-pointwise","title":"def:volume-form-pointwise","label":"def:volume-form-pointwise"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:frame-matrix","title":"def:frame-matrix","label":"def:frame-matrix"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:wedge-covectors","title":"def:wedge-covectors","label":"def:wedge-covectors"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-frame-value","title":"prop:volume-form-frame-value","label":"prop:volume-form-frame-value"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:top-forms-proportional","title":"lem:top-forms-proportional","label":"lem:top-forms-proportional"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:dual-coframe-duality","title":"lem:dual-coframe-duality","label":"lem:dual-coframe-duality"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-volume-form","title":"prop:riemannian-volume-form","label":"prop:riemannian-volume-form"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-coordinate-formula","title":"prop:volume-form-coordinate-formula","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[Lee 2.41(c): the Coordinate Formula for $dV_g$]\n\\label{prop:volume-form-coordinate-formula}\n\n\\uses{def:volume-form-pointwise, def:frame-matrix, def:wedge-covectors, prop:volume-form-frame-value, lem:top-forms-proportional, lem:dual-coframe-duality}\n\n\n\n\nIf $(Y_i)$ is positively oriented at $x$ and $(\\varepsilon^i)$ is a dual coframe there, then\n\\[\ndV_g|_x=\\sqrt{\\det(g_{ij}(x))}\\,\\varepsilon^1\\wedge\\cdots\\wedge\\varepsilon^n.\n\\]\nThus in oriented coordinates, $dV_g=\\sqrt{\\det(g_{ij})}\\,dx^1\\wedge\\cdots\\wedge dx^n$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{prop:volume-form-frame-value,lem:top-forms-proportional,def:wedge-covectors,lem:dual-coframe-duality}\n\\sketch Both sides are top forms, so compare them on $(Y_i|_x)$. The dual wedge has value $1$ there by Lemma \\ref{lem:dual-coframe-duality}; Proposition \\ref{prop:volume-form-frame-value} gives the same scalar for $dV_g$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:volume-form-pointwise","title":"def:volume-form-pointwise","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:frame-matrix","title":"def:frame-matrix","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:wedge-covectors","title":"def:wedge-covectors","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-frame-value","title":"prop:volume-form-frame-value","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:top-forms-proportional","title":"lem:top-forms-proportional","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:dual-coframe-duality","title":"lem:dual-coframe-duality","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}